> Example Benefit Eligibility Rules

This file demonstrates a simple benefit eligibility determination
encoded in Catala. Replace this with your actual legislative rules.

## Article 1: Definitions

```catala
declaration structure Individual:
  data age content integer
  data income content money
  data is_resident content boolean

declaration structure BenefitResult:
  data eligible content boolean
  data monthly_amount content money

declaration scope BenefitEligibility:
  input individual content Individual
  output result content BenefitResult
```

## Article 2: Eligibility Criteria

An individual is eligible for the benefit if they meet ALL of the
following conditions:
- They are at least 18 years old
- Their annual income is less than $30,000
- They are a resident

```catala
scope BenefitEligibility:
  definition result equals BenefitResult {
    -- eligible:
      individual.age >= 18
      and individual.income < $30,000
      and individual.is_resident
    -- monthly_amount:
      if individual.income < $15,000 then $500
      else if individual.income < $25,000 then $300
      else $150
  }
```
